# spec: set_name on the 700 sends the name as UTF-8 (é as c3 a9); the 700 answers STATUS with a 00 byte and the same bytes, twice in one read.
# source: NC 700 fw 1.8.2-11524+e0f7590, bosectl on Linux (BlueZ), notifications on; the 700's Bluetooth name then read back as the same UTF-8 bytes (NOTES.md, NC 700 section)
device nc700
call set_name Café 700
send 01 02 02 09 43 61 66 c3 a9 20 37 30 30
recv 01 02 03 0a 00 43 61 66 c3 a9 20 37 30 30 01 02 03 0a 00 43 61 66 c3 a9 20 37 30 30
result ok
